 How to search and replace the string from where the cursor is pointing?
 
 esc:s/<search-patten>/<return-pattern>
 
 s= search

Above command will replace a string where the cursor is pointing (only 1st occurance)

................................
  
 esc:s/<search-patten>/<return-pattern>/g


Above command will replace a string where the cursor is pointing (all the occurance)s

................................

 esc:5s/<search-patten>/<return-pattern>/g


Above command will replace a string in 5th line(all the occurances)

................................

 esc:5,10s/<search-patten>/<return-pattern>/g


Above command will replace a string from 5t line to 10th line (all the occurances)

................................

esc:5,10s/<search-patten>/<return-pattern>


Above command will replace a string from 5t line to 10th line (only 1st occurances)

................................

